From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.xyz>
Subject: [PATCH] net: bcmgenet: keep the TXC delay (ID mode) for rgmii-rxid

The driver turned the MAC's internal TXC delay off (ID_MODE_DIS) for
both "rgmii" and "rgmii-rxid". With "rgmii-rxid" the PHY delays only
RXC, and Linux's PHY driver turns the PHY's own TXC delay off, so the
MAC must add it: Linux (bcmmii.c) sets ID_MODE_DIS for plain "rgmii"
only. Do the same, and clear the bit otherwise.

The Raspberry Pi 4 and 400 use "rgmii-rxid". Without any TXC delay the
transmit timing is marginal: on the Pi 400, network boots failed at
random with the server holding unacknowledged data, while the Pi's MAC
counted no receive errors.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/bcmgenet.c b/drivers/net/bcmgenet.c
index fec0afd..d646c95 100644
--- a/drivers/net/bcmgenet.c
+++ b/drivers/net/bcmgenet.c
@@ -466,9 +466,15 @@ static int bcmgenet_adjust_link(struct bcmgenet_eth_priv *priv)
 	clrsetbits_32(priv->mac_reg + EXT_RGMII_OOB_CTRL, OOB_DISABLE,
 			RGMII_LINK | RGMII_MODE_EN);
 
-	if (phy_dev->interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII ||
-	    phy_dev->interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII_RXID)
+	/*
+	 * ID mode adds the 2 ns delay on TXC. Only plain "rgmii" (delays on
+	 * the board) turns it off; with "rgmii-rxid" the PHY delays RXC only,
+	 * so the MAC must still delay TXC, as in Linux (bcmmii.c).
+	 */
+	if (phy_dev->interface == PHY_INTERFACE_MODE_RGMII)
 		setbits_32(priv->mac_reg + EXT_RGMII_OOB_CTRL, ID_MODE_DIS);
+	else
+		clrbits_32(priv->mac_reg + EXT_RGMII_OOB_CTRL, ID_MODE_DIS);
 
 	writel(speed << CMD_SPEED_SHIFT, (priv->mac_reg + UMAC_CMD));
 
-- 
